       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in that profile explains the higher dose. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia.\n\nCould you clarify which of these you meant?\n\n1. **A typo or unit error.** For example, you may have meant 40 mg or 200 mg. I can enter the corrected dose right away.\n2. **A deliberate off-label dose.** If you want 400 mg/day, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional and above the usual maximum. You may also want to check the patient's other serotonergic or QT-prolonging medications.\n3. **A titration plan.** A typical start is 25\u201350 mg daily, increasing by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg. I can enter the starting dose.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter the order."
      }
